      "writtenOn": "2025-06-03T23:23:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, yeah, modules should not be allowed to modify the LRU and that\u0027s why these functions are defined in mm_inline.h. But I don\u0027t see why a module technically can\u0027t include a header from include/linux/.\nThe proper way would have been to modify this upstream but the effort failed because of the concern that the behavior will change into LIFO, see: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-mm/f29f64e29c08427b95e3df30a5770056@honor.com/, so this vendor hook approach seems the best way to handle this.",
